WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.790
Thanos may have ultimately gotten his just
desserts from the whole crew in Avengers:

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.440
Endgame, but he could have tasted defeat at
the hands of just one of Earth's Mightiest

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:08.940
Heroes.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:15.080
Chatting with ComicBook.com during San Diego
Comic-Con 2019, Marvel Studios president Kevin

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:19.279
Feige revealed that he believes an Avenger
could have defeated Josh Brolin's Mad Titan

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.480
singlehandedly had he not summoned his army
to continue fighting in his name.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.120
The hero who would have whooped Thanos' purple
butt in a one-on-one battle?

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:32.599
None other than Wanda Maximoff, aka Scarlet
Witch, whom Feige said is, quote, "probably

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:36.280
near the upper echelons of power" when it
comes to ranking the heroes of the Marvel

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.410
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.739
"I contend she would have taken down Thanos
if he hadn't called the, uh —" "Oh, she

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:42.739
had him.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:43.440
"Right, he was done."

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:47.400
Feige isn't the only one who feels Scarlet
Witch would have killed Thanos if he hadn't

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.880
started blowing up the battlefield in a desperation
move.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:51.920
"Rain fire!"

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.200
"But sire!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:54.820
Our troops!"

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.220
"Just do it!"

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.340
Avengers: Endgame co-screenwriter Stephen
McFeely and co-director Joe Russo are of the

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.970
opinion that she was Thanos' greatest adversary
on the battlefield, even sharing their thoughts

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.600
that the Mad Titan had to effectively cheat
to beat her.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.380
As McFeely said during an Endgame commentary
track,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.120
"She's really the biggest threat to Thanos
on this field."

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.220
Joe Russo agreed, saying,

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.500
"She is a very powerful character, and he
has to in a way, cheat, and sacrifice his

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.140
own armies, just to escape her."

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.340
Russo also added some more context as to where
Wanda's powers come from in the MCU, which

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.680
has always been somewhat ambiguous, especially
compared to her brother Quicksilver.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.340
As Maria Hill memorably put it in Age of Ultron,

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.540
"He's fast and she's weird."

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.100
But Joe Russo cleared things up with his Endgame
commentary, saying,

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.780
"Wanda's powers have a lot to do with her
internal life.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.780
And there's a growth to the powers and [a]
growth of her internal life and her ability

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:51.390
to harness them, and the emotion and pain
caused by Vision's death has caused an acceleration

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.040
of that growth."

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.800
As you may know, Scarlet Witch came into close
contact with Thanos at the tail end of Avengers:

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:00.740
Infinity War, when the intergalactic tyrant
was about to extract the Mind Stone from the

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.910
forehead of her lover, the Vision - all as
a part of his plan to power the Infinity Gauntlet

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.400
and wipe out half of the universe's population.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.520
Initially, Scarlet Witch made the difficult
choice to pull the Mind Stone out of Vision

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.960
herself, at his request, destroying the powerful
gem before Thanos could get his hands on it.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.680
She was successful, but Thanos used the Time
Stone to undo Scarlet Witch's actions and

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.100
snatch the Stone for himself.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:26.800
With Vision dead and Thanos' Gauntlet ready
for snapping, the Mad Titan carried out his

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.520
dastardly plan and turned Scarlet Witch and
billions of other people into space dust.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.860
Fast forward to the final battle of Avengers:
Endgame, when the formerly dusted heroes came

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.030
back to life thanks to Hulk and the Stark
Gauntlet, powered by Infinity Stones the team

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.300
collected from the past.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.700
Scarlet Witch was once again on the side of
the living, and her rage over Thanos killing

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.430
Vision was fresh in her mind — even though
this Thanos, chronologically, hadn't killed

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.220
the Vision or even met Wanda yet.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.640
Not that that mattered to her.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.830
"You took everything from me."

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.820
"I don't even know who you are."

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:01.380
"You will."

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.220
As soon as Scarlet Witch's powers proved too
much for Thanos to take, he called in his

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.590
airstrike, an assault only diverted by the
arrival of Captain Marvel, another hero whose

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.620
incredible powers stemmed from contact with
an Infinity Stone.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:18.100
The fact that Scarlet Witch could have taken
down Thanos on her own is intriguing, and

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:22.190
though Thanos isn't coming back for the MCU's
phase 4 - at least, not as far as we know

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.940
- there will be ample opportunities to explore
Wanda's powerset.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.099
She'll appear alongside Vision on the upcoming
Disney+ [disney plus] series WandaVision,

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.510
and will be a starring character in Doctor
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.960
Both projects will give fans a chance to see
Scarlet Witch at the top of her game, hopefully

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:41.060
channeling the fire and fury seen in Avengers:
Endgame.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.700
If Thanos couldn't handle her, it's hard to
guess who will.

